  "$comment": "Campaign level 16 (stretch 3, hard pass): a crown of stones. Seven capturable stones (two ley, three ward, two seer) sit on a rotationally symmetric continent, and two wolf packs den by the north seer and the southwestern ward. Staged prayer chain: take the western ley, clear both packs (which wakes the dormant crown ward), take the crown (which wakes the north seer, already held by the sneaky rival), pray the seer away, keep six of the seven stones at once for two minutes while the rival prays them back and raids, then break the eastern tribe. The rival is hard but capped at 14 troops; its village is a fort (four watchtowers, twelve posted wardens) and three more posted wardens arrive every 100 s from minute 4, so the longer the player waits the harder the last stage gets.",
